<title>USA: Beacon says buys complex for $77 mln.</title>
<headline>Beacon says buys complex for $77 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beacon Properties Corp said it has acquired a 791,000-square-foot, four-tower office complex in Chicago for $77 million.</p>
<p>The property, known as Presidents Plaza, is near O'Hare International Airport.</p>
<p>The company acquired the plaza from Metroplitan Life Insurance Co, New York in exchange for cash and operating partnership units, it said.</p>
